From 07b9864262b78912fce5c0d609387478009190b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Talaria <324092415+talaria0101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 02:50:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] add a ptrace-free tracing backend (seccomp user
 notification)

'If you can run a binary, you must be able to trace it': on hosts where
the ptrace syscall class is denied outright (sandboxed CI, hardened
environments -- ptrace, process_vm_*, PTRACE_* and /proc/pid/mem
writes all answer EPERM), the tracer now falls back to a backend built
on facilities an unprivileged tracee can always provide:

* the tracee installs a SECCOMP_FILTER_FLAG_NEW_LISTENER filter over
  every syscall before exec and hands the listener fd to the tracer
  over a unix socket; filters are inherited, so forks and execs stay
  traced;
* memory arguments are fetched through /proc/<pid>/mem while the
  tracee is blocked in the notification (stable, no TOCTOU);
* open/openat are emulated in the tracer and their fds installed with
  SECCOMP_IOCTL_NOTIF_ADDFD, so open results (including the ENOENT of
  dlopen probes -- the packager's gold) are real; access/faccessat
  likewise; everything else is CONTINUEd;
* --anti-anti-debug spoofs ptrace(TRACEME) by answering success (on
  such hosts TracerPid is genuinely 0 anyway -- no tracer link
  exists); --keep-alive answers exit_group with success.

New --backend={auto,ptrace,seccomp} option (default auto: probe ptrace,
fall back with a notice).  ucopy.c gains a /proc/<pid>/mem fallback
(read-only, reopened after execve: the fd pins the target mm) used when
both process_vm_readv and PTRACE_PEEKDATA fail.

The development sandbox (ptrace denied for every request, evidence in
experiments/logs/10-ptrace-map.txt) now runs the full validation
matrix live: tests-ext/validate.sh 25 passed / 0 failed; the
quick-sharun comparison table (experiments/logs/50-live-comparison/)
shows LD_DEBUG=libs missing the post-exit dlopen probes that this
backend records, and seeing nothing at all for static binaries.

Known limits (documented): no signal events, ret=null for CONTINUEd
syscalls, -p attach impossible, and an outer ERRNO filter outranks
USER_NOTIF (kernel action precedence) so syscalls the host denies are
never seen.
